<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert II, Duke of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1298">1298</a>–<a href="/years/1358">1358</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Albert II of Austria, Albert the Lame</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert II, called the Lame or the Wise, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> from 1330 to 1358. He added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a> to the family's lands in 1335 and governed through a long period of peace in Austria. In the west he opposed the growing Swiss Confederacy, besieging Zürich in 1351–1354 after it had joined the confederates, without success.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-ii-duke-of-austria.jpg" alt="Albert II, Duke of Austria" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_II,_Duke_of_Austria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
